/-!
# The Bernoulli laws as an exponential family

The real Bernoulli laws `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, m)` with `m ∈ (0, 1)` form the natural exponential family
(`T = id`) generated by any of them. With the base `ρ = Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)`, for example
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, 1/2)` with `η₀ = 0`, the member of natural parameter `η` is
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid (η₀ + η))`: tilting a Bernoulli law multiplies the odds `m / (1 - m)` by
`exp η`. The mean map `ψ'(η) = sigmoid (η₀ + η)` takes every value in `(0, 1)`, so the means of the
family are the interval `(0, 1)`, the member of mean `m` is `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, m)`, and the divergence
of the family in the mean parametrization is the binary relative entropy `klBerReal`.

The Cramér rate function of a Bernoulli law `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)` at a level `x ∈ [0, 1]` is the
binary relative entropy `klBer x q`, the boundary levels `0` and `1` and the boundary parameters
`q ∈ {0, 1}` included. So the extended divergence of the family is `klBer` at every level in
`[0, 1]`, and the upper confidence level of the family is the KL-UCB level `klUpper` of rewards in
`[0, 1]`, at the empirical means `0` and `1` as well.

This identifies the Chernoff bounds for exponential families with the Chernoff bounds for
Bernoulli laws in relative-entropy form.

The variance function of the family is `ψ''(η) = m (1 - m)` at the mean `m = sigmoid (η₀ + η)`,
which is also the derivative of the mean map. So the Jeffreys prior `√ψ''(η) dη` is, in the mean,
`√(m (1 - m)) dm / (m (1 - m)) = m ^ (-1 / 2) (1 - m) ^ (-1 / 2) dm`: the arcsine law
`Beta(1 / 2, 1 / 2)` times its total mass `B(1 / 2, 1 / 2) = π`. After `s` observations of sum
`S`, the likelihood `exp (η S - s ψ(η))` is a constant multiple of `m ^ S (1 - m) ^ (s - S)`, so
for `-1 / 2 < S < s + 1 / 2` the posterior of the mean is `Beta(S + 1 / 2, s - S + 1 / 2)`: the
sampling law of Thompson sampling with the Jeffreys prior for Bernoulli arms [KKM13, Figure 1].

## Main statements

* `LMLExplore.not_ae_eq_const_bernoulliMeasure`: for `q ∈ (0, 1)`, the identity is not almost
  everywhere constant under `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamily_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the member of natural parameter `η` of the
  exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid (η₀ + η))`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the means of the family are `(0, 1)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the member of mean `m ∈ (0, 1)` is
  `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, m)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyDiv_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the divergence of the family is
  `klBerReal p m` for `p, m ∈ (0, 1)`.
* `LMLExplore.rateFunction_id_bernoulliMeasure`: the rate function of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)` at a
  level `x ∈ [0, 1]` is `klBer x q`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyRate_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the extended divergence of the family is
  `klBer x m` for `x ∈ [0, 1]` and `m ∈ (0, 1)`.
* `LMLExplore.expFamilyUpper_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the upper confidence level of the family is
  `klUpper x c` for `x ∈ [0, 1]`.
* `LMLExplore.iteratedDeriv_two_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`,
  `LMLExplore.jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the variance function of the family is
  `m (1 - m)` at the mean `m = sigmoid (η₀ + η)`, and its Jeffreys prior is `√(m (1 - m)) dη`.
* `LMLExplore.map_deriv_cgf_jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid`: the image of the Jeffreys
  prior by the mean map is `π • Beta(1 / 2, 1 / 2)`.
* `LMLExplore.map_deriv_cgf_expFamilyPosterior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid_jeffreysPrior`: for
  `-1 / 2 < S < s + 1 / 2`, the image by the mean map of the posterior for the Jeffreys prior after
  `s` observations of sum `S` is `Beta(S + 1 / 2, s - S + 1 / 2)`.

## References

* [KKM13] N. Korda, E. Kaufmann and R. Munos, *Thompson sampling for 1-dimensional exponential
  family bandits*, NeurIPS 2013.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Real Set

open scoped unitInterval ENNReal

namespace LMLExplore

variable {η₀ m p x : ℝ}

/-- For `q ∈ (0, 1)`, the identity is not almost everywhere constant under `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)`:
both values `0` and `1` have positive probability. This is the nondegeneracy assumption of the mean
parametrization of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)`. -/
lemma not_ae_eq_const_bernoulliMeasure {q : I} (hq : (q : ℝ) ∈ Ioo 0 1) (c : ℝ) :
    ¬ id =ᵐ[Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)] fun _ ↦ c := by
  intro h
  -- The mean `q` and the second moment `q` would both be determined by `c`: `q = c = c²`.
  have h1 := integral_congr_ae h
  have h2 := integral_congr_ae (h.fun_comp (· ^ 2))
  simp [integral_bernoulliMeasure] at h1 h2
  nlinarith [hq.1, hq.2]

/-- Tilting a Bernoulli law multiplies its odds by `exp η`: the member of natural parameter `η` of
the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` with statistic `id` is
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid (η₀ + η))`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamily_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ η : ℝ) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamily id η =
      Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) := by
  rw [Measure.expFamily_def, tilted_bernoulliMeasure]
  congr 1
  ext
  -- `σ(η₀) exp η / (σ(η₀) exp η + 1 - σ(η₀)) = σ(η₀ + η)`
  simp only [id_eq, mul_one, mul_zero, exp_zero, unitInterval.coe_sigmoid]
  rw [div_eq_iff (add_pos (mul_pos (Real.sigmoid_pos η₀) (exp_pos η))
    (sub_pos.2 (Real.sigmoid_lt_one η₀))).ne']
  simp only [Real.sigmoid_def, exp_neg, exp_add]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- The mean map of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is
`η ↦ sigmoid (η₀ + η)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem deriv_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ η : ℝ) :
    deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀)) η = Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) := by
  rw [← Measure.integral_expFamily (by simp), expFamily_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid,
    integral_bernoulliMeasure]
  simp

/-- The means of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` are the interval
`(0, 1)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyMeans id = Ioo 0 1 := by
  have h : deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀)) = Real.sigmoid ∘ (η₀ + ·) :=
    funext (deriv_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀)
  rw [Measure.expFamilyMeans_def, integrableExpSet_bernoulliMeasure, interior_univ, image_univ, h,
    (add_left_surjective η₀).range_comp, Real.range_sigmoid]

/-- The member of mean `m ∈ (0, 1)` of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, m)`. -/
theorem expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) (hm : m ∈ Ioo 0 1) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamily id
        (Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).natParam id m) =
      Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, ⟨m, Ioo_subset_Icc_self hm⟩) := by
  have hm' : m ∈ Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyMeans id := by
    rwa [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]
  rw [expFamily_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]
  congr 1
  ext
  rw [unitInterval.coe_sigmoid, ← deriv_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid,
    Measure.deriv_cgf_natParam hm']

/-- The divergence of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` in the mean
parametrization is the binary relative entropy: `d(p, m) = klBerReal p m` for `p, m ∈ (0, 1)`. -/
theorem expFamilyDiv_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) (hp : p ∈ Ioo 0 1) (hm : m ∈ Ioo 0 1) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyDiv id p m = klBerReal p m := by
  rw [← Measure.toReal_klDiv_expFamily_natParam (by rwa [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid])
      (by rwa [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]),
    expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hp,
    expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hm, klDiv_bernoulliMeasure one_ne_zero]
  exact toReal_klBer (Ioo_subset_Icc_self hp) (Ioo_subset_Icc_self hm) (klBer_ne_top hm)

/-- **Rate function of a Bernoulli law**: the Cramér rate function of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q)` at a
level `x ∈ [0, 1]` is the binary relative entropy `d(x, q)`. At the boundary levels `0` and `1`, it
is `-log P(X = x)`; for `q ∈ {0, 1}`, the law is a Dirac mass and the rate function is infinite
away from `q`. -/
theorem rateFunction_id_bernoulliMeasure (q : I) (hx : x ∈ Icc 0 1) :
    rateFunction id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q) x = klBer x q := by
  have hae : ∀ᵐ z ∂Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q), z ∈ Icc 0 1 := by
    simpa [uIcc_of_ge zero_le_one] using ae_mem_uIcc_bernoulliMeasure (1 : ℝ) 0 q
  rcases hx.1.eq_or_lt with rfl | hx0
  · -- The level `0` is the essential infimum, of probability `1 - q`.
    have hs : {z : ℝ | id z = 0} = {0} := by ext; simp
    have hP : Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q).real {z : ℝ | id z = 0} = 1 - q := by
      rw [hs, bernoulliMeasure_real_apply_of_notMem_of_mem _ (measurableSet_singleton 0)
        (by norm_num) rfl]
    by_cases hq : (q : ℝ) = 1
    · rw [rateFunction_eq_top_of_ae_ge aemeasurable_id (hae.mono fun z hz ↦ hz.1)
        ((measureReal_eq_zero_iff).1 (by rw [hP, hq, sub_self])), eq_comm,
        klBer_eq_top_iff hx q.2]
      exact Or.inr ⟨hq, zero_ne_one⟩
    · rw [rateFunction_eq_ofReal_neg_log_measureReal_of_ae_ge aemeasurable_id
        (hae.mono fun z hz ↦ hz.1)
        (fun h ↦ sub_ne_zero.2 (Ne.symm hq) (by rw [← hP]; exact (measureReal_eq_zero_iff).2 h)),
        hP, klBer_eq_ofReal_klBerReal hx q.2 ((klBer_ne_top_iff hx q.2).2
          ⟨fun _ ↦ rfl, fun h ↦ absurd h hq⟩)]
      simp [klBerReal_def]
  rcases hx.2.eq_or_lt with rfl | hx1
  · -- The level `1` is the essential supremum, of probability `q`.
    have hs : {z : ℝ | id z = 1} = {1} := by ext; simp
    have hP : Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, q).real {z : ℝ | id z = 1} = q := by
      rw [hs, bernoulliMeasure_real_apply_of_mem_of_notMem _ (measurableSet_singleton 1) rfl
        (by norm_num)]
    by_cases hq : (q : ℝ) = 0
    · rw [rateFunction_eq_top_of_ae_le aemeasurable_id (hae.mono fun z hz ↦ hz.2)
        ((measureReal_eq_zero_iff).1 (by rw [hP, hq])), eq_comm, klBer_eq_top_iff hx q.2]
      exact Or.inl ⟨hq, one_ne_zero⟩
    · rw [rateFunction_eq_ofReal_neg_log_measureReal_of_ae_le aemeasurable_id
        (hae.mono fun z hz ↦ hz.2)
        (fun h ↦ hq (by rw [← hP]; exact (measureReal_eq_zero_iff).2 h)),
        hP, klBer_eq_ofReal_klBerReal hx q.2 ((klBer_ne_top_iff hx q.2).2
          ⟨fun h ↦ absurd h hq, fun _ ↦ rfl⟩), klBerReal_one_left]
  -- At an interior level, the law is a Dirac mass at `0` or `1`, or a member of the family.
  rcases q.2.1.eq_or_lt with hq0 | hq0
  · obtain rfl : q = 0 := Subtype.ext hq0.symm
    rw [bernoulliMeasure_zero, rateFunction_eq_top_of_ae_lt aemeasurable_id
      (by rw [ae_dirac_eq]; exact hx0), eq_comm, klBer_eq_top_iff hx (by simp)]
    exact Or.inl ⟨rfl, hx0.ne'⟩
  rcases q.2.2.eq_or_lt with hq1 | hq1
  · obtain rfl : q = 1 := Subtype.ext hq1
    rw [bernoulliMeasure_one, rateFunction_eq_top_of_ae_gt aemeasurable_id
      (by rw [ae_dirac_eq]; exact hx1), eq_comm, klBer_eq_top_iff hx (by simp)]
    exact Or.inr ⟨rfl, hx1.ne⟩
  have h := expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid 0 ⟨hq0, hq1⟩
  rw [Subtype.coe_eta] at h
  rw [← h, ← Measure.expFamilyRate_def, Measure.expFamilyRate_eq_ofReal_expFamilyDiv
      (by rw [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]; exact ⟨hx0, hx1⟩)
      (by rw [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]; exact ⟨hq0, hq1⟩),
    expFamilyDiv_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid 0 ⟨hx0, hx1⟩ ⟨hq0, hq1⟩,
    klBer_eq_ofReal_klBerReal hx q.2 (klBer_ne_top ⟨hq0, hq1⟩)]

/-- The extended divergence of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is the
binary relative entropy: `dbar(x, m) = klBer x m` for every level `x ∈ [0, 1]`, the boundary levels
included, and every mean `m ∈ (0, 1)`. -/
theorem expFamilyRate_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) (hx : x ∈ Icc 0 1) (hm : m ∈ Ioo 0 1) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyRate id x m = klBer x m := by
  rw [Measure.expFamilyRate_def, expFamily_natParam_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hm,
    rateFunction_id_bernoulliMeasure _ hx]

/-- The upper confidence level of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is the
KL-UCB level of rewards in `[0, 1]`: `U(x, c) = klUpper x c` for every level `x ∈ [0, 1]`, the
boundary levels included, and every budget `c`. -/
theorem expFamilyUpper_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) (hx : x ∈ Icc 0 1) (c : ℝ≥0∞) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyUpper id x c = (klUpper x c : EReal) := by
  have hU := klUpper_mem_Icc hx.2 c
  refine le_antisymm (Measure.expFamilyUpper_le_iff.2 ⟨EReal.coe_le_coe_iff.2 hU.1,
    fun q hq hxq hqc ↦ EReal.coe_le_coe_iff.2 ?_⟩) ?_
  · rw [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid] at hq
    rw [expFamilyRate_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hx hq] at hqc
    exact (le_klUpper_iff ⟨hxq, hq.2.le⟩).2 hqc
  rcases hU.1.eq_or_lt with h | h
  · rw [← h]
    exact Measure.le_expFamilyUpper _ _ _ _
  -- Every `r ∈ (x, klUpper x c)` is a mean with `d(x, r) ≤ c`, so it lies below `U(x, c)`.
  by_contra! hlt
  obtain ⟨r, hr, hru⟩ := EReal.lt_iff_exists_real_btwn.1 (max_lt hlt (EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff.2 h))
  rw [max_lt_iff, EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff] at hr
  have hru' := EReal.coe_lt_coe_iff.1 hru
  have hr01 : r ∈ Ioo 0 1 := ⟨hx.1.trans_lt hr.2, hru'.trans_le hU.2⟩
  refine hr.1.not_ge (Measure.le_expFamilyUpper_of_expFamilyRate_le
    (by rw [expFamilyMeans_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]; exact hr01) hr.2.le ?_)
  rw [expFamilyRate_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hx hr01]
  exact (le_klUpper_iff ⟨hr.2.le, hr01.2.le⟩).1 hru'.le

/-! ### The Jeffreys prior and its posteriors -/

section Jeffreys

variable {s : ℕ} {S : ℝ}

/-- The log-partition function of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)`:
`ψ(η) = log (1 - sigmoid η₀) - log (1 - sigmoid (η₀ + η))`. -/
private lemma cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ η : ℝ) :
    cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀) η =
      log (1 - Real.sigmoid η₀) - log (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) := by
  have h0 : 0 < 1 - Real.sigmoid η₀ := sub_pos.2 (Real.sigmoid_lt_one _)
  have h1 : 0 < 1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) := sub_pos.2 (Real.sigmoid_lt_one _)
  rw [TauCeti.Probability.cgf_id_bernoulliMeasure, unitInterval.coe_sigmoid,
    ← log_div h0.ne' h1.ne']
  congr 1
  rw [eq_div_iff h1.ne']
  simp only [Real.sigmoid_def, exp_neg, exp_add]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- The variance function of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)`: the second
derivative of its log-partition function at `η` is the variance `m (1 - m)` of the member of mean
`m = sigmoid (η₀ + η)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem iteratedDeriv_two_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ η : ℝ) :
    iteratedDeriv 2 (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀)) η =
      Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) := by
  rw [iteratedDeriv_succ, iteratedDeriv_one,
    funext (deriv_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀), deriv_comp_const_add, Real.deriv_sigmoid]

/-- The Jeffreys prior of the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` is the measure
`√(m (1 - m)) dη` on the line of natural parameters, with `m = sigmoid (η₀ + η)` the mean of the
member of natural parameter `η`. -/
theorem jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ : ℝ) :
    Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).jeffreysPrior id = volume.withDensity fun η ↦
      ENNReal.ofReal √(Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η))) := by
  simp [Measure.jeffreysPrior_def, integrableExpSet_bernoulliMeasure]

/-- The unnormalized posterior density of the exponential family of
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` for its Jeffreys prior, after `s` observations of sum `S`, is
`m (1 - m)` times `C m ^ (S - 1 / 2) (1 - m) ^ (s - S - 1 / 2)` at the mean
`m = sigmoid (η₀ + η)`, with `C = exp (-η₀ S - s log (1 - sigmoid η₀))`. -/
private lemma sqrt_mul_exp_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (η₀ η S : ℝ) (s : ℕ) :
    √(Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η))) *
        exp (η * S - s * cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀) η) =
      Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) *
        (exp (-(η₀ * S) - s * log (1 - Real.sigmoid η₀)) *
          (Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) ^ (S - 1 / 2) *
            (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) ^ ((s : ℝ) - S - 1 / 2))) := by
  rw [cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]
  have hη : η = log (Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) - log (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) - η₀ := by
    rw [← log_div (Real.sigmoid_pos _).ne' (sub_pos.2 (Real.sigmoid_lt_one _)).ne',
      Real.log_sigmoid_div_one_sub]
    ring
  set m := Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)
  have hm0 : 0 < m := Real.sigmoid_pos _
  have hm1 : 0 < 1 - m := sub_pos.2 (Real.sigmoid_lt_one _)
  have hm : m * (1 - m) = exp (log m + log (1 - m)) := by
    rw [exp_add, exp_log hm0, exp_log hm1]
  rw [hm, sqrt_eq_rpow, rpow_def_of_pos (exp_pos _), rpow_def_of_pos hm0,
    rpow_def_of_pos hm1, log_exp, ← exp_add, ← exp_add, ← exp_add, ← exp_add]
  congr 1
  rw [hη]
  ring

variable (η₀ : ℝ)

/-- The image by the mean map of the Jeffreys prior of the exponential family of
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` weighted by the likelihood of `s` observations of sum `S`, for
`-1 / 2 < S < s + 1 / 2`: a positive finite multiple of `Beta(S + 1 / 2, s - S + 1 / 2)`. -/
private lemma map_deriv_cgf_withDensity_jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid
    (hS0 : -(1 / 2) < S) (hS1 : S < s + 1 / 2) :
    ((Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).jeffreysPrior id).withDensity fun η ↦
          ENNReal.ofReal (exp (η * S - s * cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀) η))).map
        (deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀))) =
      ENNReal.ofReal (exp (-(η₀ * S) - s * log (1 - Real.sigmoid η₀)) *
          beta (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2)) • betaMeasure (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2) := by
  have hα : 0 < S + 1 / 2 := by linarith
  have hβ : 0 < (s : ℝ) - S + 1 / 2 := by linarith
  have hB := beta_pos hα hβ
  set C := exp (-(η₀ * S) - s * log (1 - Real.sigmoid η₀))
  set g := ENNReal.ofReal (C * beta (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2)) •
    betaPDF (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2)
  -- the mean map `η ↦ σ(η₀ + η)` carries the density `|σ'(η₀ + η)| g(σ(η₀ + η))` on the line to
  -- the density `g` on `(0, 1)`
  have hmap := TauCeti.MeasureTheory.map_withDensity_abs_deriv_mul
    (φ := fun η ↦ Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) (f := g) MeasurableSet.univ
    (continuous_sigmoid.comp (continuous_const_add η₀)).measurable
    (fun η _ ↦ ((Real.hasDerivAt_sigmoid (η₀ + η)).comp_const_add η₀ η).hasDerivWithinAt)
    (Real.sigmoid_strictMono.comp (strictMono_id.const_add η₀)).injective.injOn
  have hrange : range (fun η ↦ Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) = Ioo 0 1 := by
    rw [← Real.range_sigmoid]
    exact (add_left_surjective η₀).range_comp Real.sigmoid
  rw [Measure.restrict_univ, image_univ, hrange] at hmap
  -- the posterior weight of the Jeffreys prior is that density, for a multiple `g` of the beta
  -- density
  have hdens : (fun η ↦ ENNReal.ofReal √(Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η))) *
        ENNReal.ofReal
          (exp (η * S - s * cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀) η))) =
      fun η ↦ ENNReal.ofReal |Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η) * (1 - Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η))| *
        g (Real.sigmoid (η₀ + η)) := by
    ext η
    have hm0 := Real.sigmoid_pos (η₀ + η)
    have hm1 := Real.sigmoid_lt_one (η₀ + η)
    simp only [g, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    rw [abs_of_nonneg (mul_nonneg hm0.le (sub_nonneg.2 hm1.le)), betaPDF_of_pos_lt_one hm0 hm1,
      ← ENNReal.ofReal_mul (sqrt_nonneg _), sqrt_mul_exp_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid,
      ← ENNReal.ofReal_mul (mul_pos (exp_pos _) hB).le,
      ← ENNReal.ofReal_mul (mul_nonneg hm0.le (sub_nonneg.2 hm1.le))]
    congr 2
    rw [show S + 1 / 2 - 1 = S - 1 / 2 by ring,
      show (s : ℝ) - S + 1 / 2 - 1 = s - S - 1 / 2 by ring]
    generalize beta (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2) = B at hB ⊢
    field_simp
  rw [jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid, ← withDensity_mul _ (by fun_prop) ?_,
    Pi.mul_def, hdens, funext (deriv_cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀), hmap,
    withDensity_smul' _ _ ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top,
    ← TauCeti.Probability.betaMeasure_eq_withDensity_restrict_Ioo]
  simp_rw [cgf_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid]
  fun_prop

/-- The Jeffreys prior of the Bernoulli family is the arcsine law `Beta(1 / 2, 1 / 2)` on the mean,
up to its total mass `π`: the image of the Jeffreys prior of the exponential family of
`Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` by the mean map `ψ'(η) = sigmoid (η₀ + η)` is
`π • Beta(1 / 2, 1 / 2)` [KKM13, Section 2]. -/
theorem map_deriv_cgf_jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid :
    (Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).jeffreysPrior id).map
        (deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀))) =
      ENNReal.ofReal π • betaMeasure (1 / 2) (1 / 2) := by
  have h := map_deriv_cgf_withDensity_jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid (s := 0) (S := 0) η₀
    (by norm_num) (by norm_num)
  have hbeta : beta (1 / 2) (1 / 2) = π := by
    norm_num [beta, Gamma_one_half_eq, mul_self_sqrt pi_pos.le]
  simp only [CharP.cast_eq_zero, mul_zero, zero_mul, sub_zero, neg_zero, exp_zero, zero_add,
    one_mul, ENNReal.ofReal_one, hbeta] at h
  rwa [← Pi.one_def, withDensity_one] at h

/-- **The posterior of the Bernoulli family for the Jeffreys prior is a beta law** [KKM13,
Figure 1]: after `s` observations of sum `S` with `-1 / 2 < S < s + 1 / 2` (for example `s`
Bernoulli observations with `S` successes), the image of the posterior of the natural parameter of
the exponential family of `Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, sigmoid η₀)` for its Jeffreys prior by the mean map
`ψ'(η) = sigmoid (η₀ + η)` is `Beta(S + 1 / 2, s - S + 1 / 2)`. -/
theorem map_deriv_cgf_expFamilyPosterior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid_jeffreysPrior
    (hS0 : -(1 / 2) < S) (hS1 : S < s + 1 / 2) :
    (Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).expFamilyPosterior id
          (Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).jeffreysPrior id) s S).map
        (deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀))) =
      betaMeasure (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2) := by
  have := isProbabilityMeasureBeta (α := S + 1 / 2) (β := s - S + 1 / 2) (by linarith)
    (by linarith)
  have hf : Measurable (deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀))) :=
    measurable_deriv _
  set μ := (Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀).jeffreysPrior id).withDensity fun η ↦
    ENNReal.ofReal (exp (η * S - s * cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀) η))
  have hμ : μ Set.univ = μ.map (deriv (cgf id Ber((1 : ℝ), 0, unitInterval.sigmoid η₀)))
      Set.univ := by
    rw [Measure.map_apply hf MeasurableSet.univ, preimage_univ]
  have hc0 : ENNReal.ofReal (exp (-(η₀ * S) - s * log (1 - Real.sigmoid η₀)) *
      beta (S + 1 / 2) (s - S + 1 / 2)) ≠ 0 :=
    (ENNReal.ofReal_pos.2 (mul_pos (exp_pos _) (beta_pos (by linarith) (by linarith)))).ne'
  rw [Measure.expFamilyPosterior_def, integrableExpSet_bernoulliMeasure, interior_univ,
    ProbabilityTheory.cond, Measure.restrict_univ, Measure.map_smul, hμ,
    map_deriv_cgf_withDensity_jeffreysPrior_bernoulliMeasure_sigmoid η₀ hS0 hS1,
    smul_apply, measure_univ, smul_eq_mul, mul_one, smul_smul,
    ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel hc0 ENNReal.ofReal_ne_top, one_smul]
  exact hf.aemeasurable

